# The CD intro is captured at HNM frame 40 by the harness. These commands
# exercise the landing screen (throne room), room rendering, a tap on the
# first command row ("SEE DUNE MAP" opens the globe), and a clean engine exit.
#
# Comments after '#' on a command line say what a click hits and what a
# wait lets finish; scripts/dune_script_trace.py prints what each line did.
wait 1000               # the intro (captured at HNM frame 40) to the throne room
checkpoint cd-landing
checkpoint cd-room-scripted
move 160 163
click left 160 163      # row 1: SEE DUNE MAP: the flat map
wait 5000               # the map draws with its DUNE MAP popup
checkpoint cd-after-touch
# EXIT MAPS (the first row) returns to the throne room.
move 160 163
click left 160 163      # row 1: EXIT MAPS: back to the throne room
wait 1000               # the room draws
# Paul's head opens the globe with the game menu; SAVE GAME (third row)
# lists Log 1, Log 2 and Cancel, as the original does. Cancel returns to the
# menu, EXIT GLOBE (first row) to the flat map and EXIT MAPS to the room.
move 160 155            # the pointer (the checkpoint records the cursor)
click left 160 155      # the box's top edge under Paul's head: the globe
wait 4000               # the globe opens
checkpoint cd-globe
move 160 179
click left 160 179      # row 3: SAVE GAME: the save list
wait 1500               # the list opens
checkpoint cd-menu-save
move 160 179
click left 160 179      # row 3: Cancel: back to the globe menu
wait 1500               # the menu comes back
move 160 163
click left 160 163      # row 1: EXIT GLOBE: the flat map
wait 3000               # the map draws
move 160 163
click left 160 163      # row 1: EXIT MAPS: back to the throne room
wait 1500               # the room draws
# Duke Leto's opening conversation: the third command row (the CD's rows
# are SEE DUNE MAP, Mixer Panel, DUKE LETO ATREIDES), then a tap per page
# (view area) until the throne room returns.
move 160 179
click left 160 179      # row 3: DUKE LETO ATREIDES: “I am the Duke Leto Atreides, your father”
wait 1500               # Leto's first line shows
checkpoint cd-leto-1
move 160 80
click left 160 80       # view: next line “My son, we must mine the spice…”
wait 1500               # the line shows
checkpoint cd-leto-2
click left 160 80       # view: next line “We've spotted three troops of Fremen…”
wait 1500               # the line shows
checkpoint cd-leto-3
click left 160 80       # view, after the last line: closes the talk
wait 1000               # back to the throne room
quit
